C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Water Resources Systems Analysis
      HW 6 GAMS Dual solution for irrigation problem
       
      THE PROBLEM:
       
      Deciding how water should be allocated to different crops.  Data are as fol-lows:
       
      Seasonal Resource
      Inputs for Profit        Crops        Resource
      Availability
                      Hay        Grain
      June          2 acft/acre        1 acft/acre               14,000 acft
      July          1 acft/acre        2 acft/acre               18,000 acft
      August        1 acft/acre        0 acft/acre               6,000 acft
      Total Plants  1 acre             1 acre                    10,000 acres
      Return $/acre        $100        $120
       
                      Determine the optimal planting for the two crops.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Spencer Young
      a02307423@aggies.usu.edu
      October 22, 2025
  28   
  29  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  30  SETS plant crops growing /Hay, Grain/
  31       month months /June, July, August, Total/;
  32   
  33  * 2. DEFINE input data
  34  PARAMETERS
  35     c(plant) Objective function coefficients ($ per plant)
  36           /Hay 100,
  37           Grain 120/
  38     b(month) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  39            /June 14000,
  40             July  18000,
  41             August  6000,
  42             Total 10000/;
  43   
  44  TABLE A(plant,month) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  45                   June    July    August    Total
  46   Hay             2        1        1         1
  47   Grain           1        2        0         1;
  48   
  49   
  50  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  51  VARIABLES X(plant) plants planted (Number)
  52            VPROFIT  total profit ($)
  53            Y(month) planting months
  54            VRED Reduce Acerage used;
  55   
  56  * Non-negativity constraints
  57  POSITIVE VARIABLES X, Y;
  58   
  59  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  60  EQUATIONS
  61     PROFIT_PRIMAL Total profit ($) and objective function value
  62     WATER_CONSTRAINT_PRIMAL(month) Water Constraint by month
  63     REDUCE_DUAL Reduce the acerage used each month
  64     PLANT_CONSTRAINT_DUAL(plant) Constraint of the value of the plant
  65   
  66  ;
  67   
  68  * Primal
  69  PROFIT_PRIMAL..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(plant, c(plant)*X(plant));
  70  WATER_CONSTRAINT_PRIMAL(month) ..    SUM(plant, A(plant,month)*X(plant)) =L= b(month);
  71   
  72  *Dual
  73  REDUCE_DUAL  ..                 VRED =E= SUM(month, b(month)*Y(month));
  74  PLANT_CONSTRAINT_DUAL(plant)  ..             SUM(month, A(plant,month)*Y(month)) =G= c(plant);
  75   
  76  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  77  MODEL PLANTING /REDUCE_DUAL, PLANT_CONSTRAINT_DUAL/;
  78   
  79   
  80   
  81  * 6. SOLVE the MODEL
  82  * Solve the PLANTING model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  83  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  84  SOLVE PLANTING USING LP MINIMIZING VRED;
  85   
  86  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file


